I do want to say there is one thing in here I really didn't like.
我确实想说，这里有一件事我真的很不喜欢。

00:54:15.329 --> 00:54:31.449
I just want to say it because we're kind of owning some things and there's a moment in here where Barney makes reference to like a prostitute where he uses a disparaging word for the trans community that I think 20 years ago, we were too young and ignorant to realize you should not say.
我只是想把它说出来，因为我们在正视一些事情，这里有一个时刻，巴尼提到了一个类似妓女的词，他用了一个对跨性别群体带有贬义的词，我认为20年前，我们太年轻、太无知，没意识到不应该说这个词。

00:54:31.449 --> 00:54:33.889
And it is a show of love, it is a show of heart.
这是一部充满爱的剧，这是一部充满内涵的剧。

00:54:33.889 --> 00:54:37.210
This was a rare moment where I think we got it wrong.
这是一个罕见的时刻，我认为我们做错了。

00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:42.690
And I think like looking back 20 years later, it just feels important to own some of those moments.
我觉得20年后再回头看，正视其中的某些时刻显得尤为重要。

00:54:42.690 --> 00:54:46.250
I think at the time it was like, oh, there's sort of a, it's like a comedy thing.
我想当时大家的态度是，哦，这有点像，这就像是一个喜剧梗。

00:54:46.250 --> 00:54:50.730
You can say it, no, it's not a good comedy where it's not an acceptable thing to say.
你可以说，不，这不是一个好笑的喜剧，这不是一个可以接受的说法。

00:54:50.730 --> 00:55:01.090
And I wanted to especially say it because of our beautiful opening message from that, how I met your mother, a fan who said he feels so seen, he has autism, he has cerebral palsy, he's a person living with those challenges.
我想特别提一下这件事，因为我们收到了来自《老爸老妈浪漫史》粉丝的一条美妙的开场留言，他说他感到了被看见，他有自闭症，有脑瘫，是一个正在经历这些挑战的人。

00:55:01.090 --> 00:55:15.250
I became a parent of a kid with a disability between year two and year three of how much your mother, Pam, many deep talks were had, many talk about Pam knowing what people need and getting people through the hard times to still do the work, you were that for me, very much in that moment.
在《老爸老妈浪漫史》第二年到第三年之间，我成了一个残疾孩子的家长，帕姆，我们有过很多次深度的交谈，谈到帕姆懂得人们需要什么，帮助大家度过艰难时期并继续坚持工作，在那一刻，你对我也正是如此。

00:55:15.250 --> 00:55:26.610
And just the way that changed my perspective on using certain words as if they're okay, comedy words, the disability community has very strong opinions about that.
还有这种改变我观点的方式，关于使用某些词汇时觉得它们没问题，比如那些喜剧笑料里的词，残疾人群体对此有着非常强烈的看法。

00:55:26.610 --> 00:55:34.010
And I've learned so much about that and looking back on how maybe in my 20s or being in comedy veterans rooms, words are thrown about.
我对此了解了很多，回想起我在二十多岁时，或者在老派喜剧编剧室里，那些随口抛出的词汇。

00:55:34.010 --> 00:55:43.409
