And for the last section of the show, we like to close out with a letter, a written letter.
至于节目的最后一个环节，我们喜欢用一封信，一封手写的信来收尾。

01:06:57.439 --> 01:07:02.376
We often open the show with a voice note and we close with a written letter.
我们通常用语音便签开场，然后用一封写好的信收尾。

01:07:02.376 --> 01:07:38.755
If you would like to contribute either, please go to how we made your mother dot com you can also go to h y no h w m y m h w m y m that's a dot com and go to contact and just follow the links it should be pretty clear if you want to submit something we love to hear from you we love to hear what the show is meant to you and why you're still watching it after all these years if you're showing your kids like all the stuff we love it all so I just got back from Ecuador I was in Ecuador for a couple days for a Comic Con down there that was totally delightful.
如果你想贡献其中任何一个，请访问 how we made your mother dot com，你也可以访问 h y no h w m y m h w m y m，也就是点com，然后点击联系方式，按照链接操作，如果你想提交一些东西，应该会很清楚，我们喜欢听取你们的意见，我们喜欢听听这部剧对你们意味着什么，为什么历经这么多年你们还在看它，如果你把这部剧推荐给你的孩子们，所有这些，我们都非常喜欢，所以我刚从厄瓜多尔回来，我在厄瓜多尔待了几天，去那里的漫展，那真的非常愉快。

01:07:38.579 --> 01:07:59.960
I just loved being down in Guayaquil, is that, I think that's where I was, but the people were so wonderful and the enthusiasm for the show and, you know, wonderfully for me, for other stuff I've made, but it was really wonderful to connect with so many how I met your mother fans.
我特别喜欢瓜亚基尔，是这样吗，我想我当时就在那里，但那里的人们太好了，对这部剧的热情，你知道，令我惊喜的是，还有我制作的其他作品，能与这么多《老爸老妈的浪漫史》粉丝交流真的非常美妙。

01:07:59.960 --> 01:08:08.639
I think Craig, doing this show has, you know, when Pam said I'm a fan too, like it's really helping me become a fan of the show.
我觉得克雷格，做这个节目，你知道的，当帕姆说我也是个粉丝时，这真的帮我成了一个节目的粉丝。

01:08:08.639 --> 01:08:36.140
I mean, I was a fan while we were making it, but it was so, it's so hard when you're so up close to it, I'm just finding the distance from it in the years, have really softened my ability to look at it with like fresh and loving eyes, and also really appreciate when people, I mean, I can't tell you the amount of people who said, this changed my life, this show taught me everything about love and the opening testimonial we got.
我的意思是，我们在制作的时候我是个粉丝，但当你身处其中时太难了，我只是发现时间的距离和岁月的沉淀，真的让我能够用崭新而充满爱意的目光去看待它，并且真正感激当人们——我的意思是，我无法告诉你有多少人说过，这改变了我的生活，这部剧教会了我关于爱的一切，以及我们收到的开场感言。

01:08:36.140 --> 01:08:43.000
I'm so perpetually moved, and it does sound like people are saying maybe the same thing, it's not.
我永远都感动不已，听起来大家好像都在说同样的话，其实不然。

01:08:43.000 --> 01:08:47.439
If you listen, there's a lot of different varieties of this theme, but the theme holds true.
如果你仔细听，这个主题有很多不同的变体，但主题始终如一。

01:08:47.439 --> 01:08:55.047
This show met me at the right moment, a woman told me after a suicide attempt, this was the show that pulled her out of her depression.
这部剧在最恰当的时刻走进了我的生活，一位女士在一次自杀未遂后告诉我，是这部剧把她从抑郁中拉了出来。

01:08:55.047 --> 01:09:08.572
You don't realize that when you're making a comedy that has some heart to it, that feels honest, that also has some big laughs, some people you want to spend time with, it's life affirming in the deepest way and people want to return to it.
当你制作一部既走心、真诚、又能带来欢笑、里面有你想与之共度时光的人的喜剧时，你不会意识到它具有最深层的抚慰人心的力量，人们总是想要重温它。

01:09:08.572 --> 01:09:09.924
They want to spend time.
他们想要共度时光。

01:09:09.924 --> 01:09:14.319
It makes you feel like this Earth place is hard, but it's an okay place to be.
它让你觉得地球这个地方虽然艰难，但还是个挺不错的地方。

01:09:14.960 --> 01:09:19.920
Yeah, and it sounds like a prepackaged idea, that idea of, oh, it belongs to the fans now.
是的，这听起来像是一个预先包装好的概念，那种“哦，它现在属于粉丝了”的想法。

01:09:19.920 --> 01:09:23.760
I really understand how profound that is at this point.
到了这个时候，我真的深刻理解了这句话的含义。

01:09:23.760 --> 01:09:26.560
I've heard Mark Hamill talk about in interviews about Star Wars.
我听马克·哈米尔在采访中谈到过《星球大战》。

01:09:26.560 --> 01:09:31.600
He's like, I'm just honored to talk about this thing with the people it belongs to now.
他说，我很荣幸能和这些现在拥有这部作品的人谈论它。

01:09:31.600 --> 01:09:35.520
And it's like, that's how much mother is now and what an honor that it books.
这就好比现在的“老爸老妈”一样，这是一种多么大的荣幸啊。

01:09:35.520 --> 01:09:38.239
And it belongs to everyone in a different way.
它以不同的方式属于每一个人。

01:09:38.239 --> 01:09:39.520
It meets them in some different way.
它在不同的方面触动了他们。

01:09:39.520 --> 01:09:43.520
And I'm really understanding that because of this podcast, I think, at an under duper level.
我想，正是因为这个播客，我正在以一种更深层次的方式理解这一点。

01:09:43.520 --> 01:09:52.319
If someone comes up to us and says, I've watched the show 20 times front to back, There can be no question, they know the show better than we know it.
如果有人走过来对我们说，我从头到尾看了这部剧20遍，毫无疑问，他们对这部剧的了解比我们还深。

01:09:52.319 --> 01:09:53.319
They know it.
他们太懂了。

01:09:53.319 --> 01:10:02.960
Remember when I said, oh, why'd they cut that line, nerds who suck at math, life's gonna be rough boys.
还记得我说过吗，“哦，他们为什么要剪掉那句台词，不擅长数学的书呆子们，生活会很难过的，男孩们。”

01:10:02.960 --> 01:10:04.800
I thought it was outside the club.
我以为那是俱乐部外面的事。

01:10:04.800 --> 01:10:06.880
And all these people were like, that's from Best Prom Ever.
然后所有这些人都在说，那是出自《史上最佳毕业舞会》。

01:10:06.880 --> 01:10:07.880
You know, like they know immediately.
你知道的，他们立刻就知道了。

01:10:07.880 --> 01:10:08.880
That's Best Prom Ever.
那是《史上最佳毕业舞会》。

01:10:08.880 --> 01:10:09.880
I know.
我知道。

01:10:09.880 --> 01:10:10.880
I didn't catch that at her either.
我当时也没注意到她的那个。

01:10:10.880 --> 01:10:11.880
I know.
我知道。

01:10:11.880 --> 01:10:12.880
I know.
我知道。

01:10:12.880 --> 01:10:14.600
I've been corrected on that since, too.
之后我也因此被人纠正过。

01:10:14.600 --> 01:10:15.600
Yeah.
是的。

01:10:15.600 --> 01:10:26.399
I think I mentioned this, but when Selena Gomez posted just how I met your mother on her laptop, just the five of us sitting around talking at the bar, and I wrote in, what episode is this?
我想我提过这个，当赛琳娜·戈麦斯在她的笔记本电脑上播放《老爸老妈的浪漫史》时，正是我们五个人坐在酒吧里聊天的画面，我留言问，这是哪一集？

01:10:26.399 --> 01:10:27.375
Because I was curious.
因为我很好奇。

01:10:27.375 --> 01:10:29.281
And all these people wrote back, they knew.
结果所有这些人都回信了，他们都知道。

01:10:29.281 --> 01:10:30.079
How did they know?
他们怎么知道的？

01:10:30.960 --> 01:10:33.117
Our clothes that we were wearing.
凭我们当时穿的衣服。

01:10:33.117 --> 01:10:34.489
That's how they knew.
他们就是这么知道的。

01:10:34.489 --> 01:10:37.235
Because there was just beers on the table.
因为桌上只有啤酒。

01:10:37.235 --> 01:10:39.326
There was nothing signifying it.
没有什么明显的标志。

01:10:39.326 --> 01:10:40.699
I mean, just bananas.
我的意思是，太疯狂了。

01:10:40.699 --> 01:10:41.679
I just love it.
我太喜欢了。

01:10:41.680 --> 01:10:45.279
Kimmy and the fans are the best and the smartest and the coolest.
基米和粉丝们是最棒的、最聪明的、最酷的。

01:10:45.279 --> 01:10:48.119
Yeah, so I met a ton of them in Ecuador.
是的，我在厄瓜多尔遇到了成千上万的粉丝。

01:10:48.119 --> 01:10:57.079
I had such a lovely time and someone handed me this note and I only read it later, either later that night or the next day.
我度过了一段非常美好的时光，有人把这张便签递给了我，我是后来才看的，要么是那天深夜，要么是第二天。

01:10:57.079 --> 01:10:59.119
Okay, I've not heard it, lay it on us.
好吧，我还没听过，快念给我们听听。

01:10:59.119 --> 01:11:09.159
This is someone who wrote me in Ecuador and hand-delivered me this note and this is what they said, hi, Josh, you don't know me but I wanted to write this letter from the bottom of my heart.
这是我在厄瓜多尔时有人写给我并亲手交给我的一封信，内容是这样的：嗨，乔治，你可能不认识我，但我还是想发自内心地写下这封信。

01:11:09.159 --> 01:11:18.539
I'm a content creator from Ecuador, not just a fan of yours, but someone who truly admires the beautiful person you are and how your character Ted Mosby has deeply influenced my life.
我是厄瓜多尔的一名内容创作者，不仅仅是你的粉丝，更是一个真心钦佩你这个美好的人、以及你的角色泰德·莫斯比如何深刻影响我生活的人。

01:11:18.539 --> 01:11:23.060
I have dreamed of meeting you for a long time, mostly because of someone very special to me.
我梦想见到你很久了，主要是因为一个对我很特别的人。

01:11:23.060 --> 01:11:24.560
His name was Alejandro.
他叫亚历杭德罗。

01:11:24.560 --> 01:11:28.720
He was a mechatronics engineer who worked at Unilever.
他是一名在联合利华工作的机电工程师。

01:11:28.720 --> 01:11:34.600
And earlier this year in January, he tragically passed away in the ocean, caught in a whirlpool.
今年年初的1月，他不幸在海洋中遭遇漩涡而离世。

01:11:34.600 --> 01:11:36.479
Alejandro wasn't just a friend.
亚历杭德罗不仅仅是一个朋友。

01:11:36.479 --> 01:11:43.119
He was someone I loved, first as a teenage partner when I was 15, and later as a truly close friend.
他是我深爱的人，最初在我15岁时是少年的伴侣，后来成了真正亲密的朋友。

01:11:43.119 --> 01:11:45.840
One of the strongest bonds we shared was how I met your mother.
我们之间最深的羁绊之一就是《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

01:11:45.840 --> 01:11:50.520
He introduced me to the show, and for years we'd talk about it, especially about Ted.
是他带我入坑这部剧的，多年来我们一直在讨论它，尤其是关于泰德。

01:11:50.520 --> 01:11:58.840
We saw ourselves in him, always torn between wanting to be with someone, learning to be alone, and holding onto the hope of a beautiful love.
我们在他身上看到了自己的影子，总是在渴望与某人在一起、学会独自一人、以及对美好爱情的希望之间挣扎。

01:11:58.840 --> 01:12:08.680
We often talked about how Ted's journey mirrored so much of what we were learning in life, emotional growth, letting go, timing, heartbreak, and still believing in love no matter what.
我们经常谈论泰德的旅程如何反映了我们在生活中学到的很多东西：情感成长、放手、时机、心碎，以及无论如何依然相信爱情。

01:12:08.680 --> 01:12:15.920
Thank you for giving life to a character who wasn't perfect, but who grew, who let go, who learned, who hoped.
感谢你赋予了一个并不完美、但却在成长、在放手、在学习、在抱有希望的角色以生命。

01:12:15.920 --> 01:12:19.960
Thank you for showing that love is not always linear but always worth it.
谢谢你向我们展示了爱情并不总是笔直的，但永远都值得。

01:12:21.020 --> 01:12:27.420
That friends can heal you, that change is constant and that trusting love is always a brave thing to do.
朋友可以治愈你，变化是不变的，而对爱情保持信任永远是一件勇敢的事。

01:12:27.420 --> 01:12:31.779
I admire you deeply, Josh, not just as an actor but as a human being.
我深深地钦佩你，乔治，不仅仅作为一名演员，更作为一个真正的人。

01:12:31.779 --> 01:12:34.579
Thank you for being here and thank you for coming to Ecuador.
谢谢你来到这里，谢谢你来到厄瓜多尔。

01:12:34.579 --> 01:12:37.939
It's a beautiful country full of warmth and magic.
这是一个充满温暖和魔力的美丽国家。

01:12:37.939 --> 01:12:40.420
I truly hope you get to experience more of it.
我真心希望你能体验到更多这里的风情。

01:12:40.420 --> 01:12:43.739
This letter is part of my way of honoring Alejandro.
这封信是我纪念亚历杭德罗的方式的一部分。

01:12:43.739 --> 01:12:51.100
I know wherever he is, he's probably jumping with joy, knowing I got to do this to meet you, a dream we shared.
我知道无论他在哪里，他可能都在高兴得直跳，因为知道我做到了这一切——见到了你，这是我们共同的梦想。

01:12:51.100 --> 01:13:00.739
I hope this letter brings you even a fraction of what your work has meant to me with love and admiration, Millie Michon.
希望这封信能带给你一丝慰藉，让你知道你的作品对我有多大意义。带着爱与崇敬，米莉·米雄。

01:13:00.739 --> 01:13:03.659
My gosh, that's unbelievable.
天哪，这太难以置信了。

01:13:03.659 --> 01:13:05.460
That's so beautiful, thank you for that letter.
太美了，谢谢你分享这封信。

01:13:05.460 --> 01:13:08.819
like I love love isn't always linear, but it's always worth it.
就像我说的，爱情并不总是笔直的，但永远值得。

01:13:08.819 --> 01:13:10.020
It's incredible.
这太不可思议了。

01:13:10.020 --> 01:13:13.619
It's incredibly well written letter in addition to just being so nice of them to share.
除了他们分享的这份善意，这是一封写得极其出色的信。

01:13:13.619 --> 01:13:17.659
Yeah, quite beautiful, like quite a soulful person.
是的，挺美的，就像是一个很有灵魂的人。

01:13:17.659 --> 01:13:28.449
And yeah, just, you know, I hear from people like, we fell in love over the show or my friend and I went deeper in our friendship because of this show.
而且，你知道的，我经常听到有人说，我们因为这部剧而坠入爱河，或者我和朋友因为这部剧加深了友谊。

01:13:28.449 --> 01:13:35.595
And, you know, I also, I really love at the time, time, it was hard for me to play such a vulnerable, flawed character.
而且，你知道，我也真的很喜欢——当时，对我来说，扮演这样一个脆弱、有缺陷的角色其实很难。

01:13:35.595 --> 01:13:40.459
I felt like I had to let people see these, you know, it was me and not me, right?
我觉得我不得不让人们看到这些，你知道的，那是“我”又不是“我”，对吧？

01:13:40.459 --> 01:13:48.745
I had to let them see these parts of me that I was little like, or a little embarrassed about or a little like, no, these are parts of me.
我不得不让他们看到我身上这些部分，其实我心里有点……或者有点尴尬，或者觉得，不，这些都是我的一部分。

01:13:48.745 --> 01:13:50.786
I don't reveal all that regularly.
我并不经常把这些展现出来。

01:13:50.786 --> 01:13:55.109
But then I was asked to do it in front of millions of people every week.
但随后我却被要求每周在数百万观众面前这样做。

01:13:55.109 --> 01:14:08.109
And to now see 20 years later that that's the very thing that people latch on to and respond to and love so much, his imperfections.
而现在，20年后看到，正是这一点让人们紧紧抓住、产生共鸣并如此喜爱，也就是他的不完美。

01:14:08.109 --> 01:14:14.109
I've said this quote, but when we talk about our accomplishments, it breeds competition.
我说过这样一句话，当我们谈论我们的成就时，它会滋生竞争。

01:14:14.109 --> 01:14:17.109
When we talk about our vulnerability, it breeds community.
当我们谈论我们的脆弱时，它会滋生社群。

01:14:17.109 --> 01:14:28.960
So, I think there's, there's just, you know, Ted is like, I think he's a classic character because he was so wrong so often, you know, he was so much like us.
所以，我觉得，你知道的，泰德就像是一个经典角色，因为他经常犯错，你知道的，他跟我们太像了。

01:14:28.960 --> 01:14:32.239
He was, he was, he was drawing erroneous conclusions.
他总是得出错误的结论。

01:14:32.239 --> 01:14:40.239
He was thinking the paralegal was a prostitute, you know, he was just constantly stepping on Rakes to reference the Simpsons we were talking about earlier.
他以为那个律所助理是个妓女，你知道的，他就像我们刚才提到的《辛普森一家》那样，不断地踩钉耙。

01:14:40.239 --> 01:14:46.180
But he also, he, he, he believed in, in, in love, he believed in his friends.
但同时，他也相信爱，相信他的朋友。

01:14:46.180 --> 01:15:07.770
He ultimately ends up believing in himself and it was an honor and an honor to have played a part in people's lives, I can't overstate that.
他最终开始相信自己，能够在人们的生活中扮演这样一个角色是一种荣幸，对此我怎么强调都不为过。

